CORE libcxx
views_iota.cpp
--cpp20 --stdlib libc++ --object-bits 12 --unwind 8
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ iota: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of system-header function
--
libc++ (LLVM 18) std::views::iota.  The layers that broke it: iterator_concept
from derived_from on incomplete classes
(cpp11_conversion_between_incomplete_classes) and __make_signed's result
type (cpp20_builtin_make_signed_corresponding_type), which made the
__iterator constructor lose its body.  clang++ 18 -stdlib=libc++ accepts this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
